{"name":"Billet","hex":"#ad7c35","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"billet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A short informal letter.","A written order to quarter soldiers."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where a soldier is assigned to lodge.","Temporary lodgings in a private residence, such as is organised for members of a visiting sports team."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/billet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Billet","blocks":[{"text":"In European militaries, a billet is a living-quarters to which a soldier is assigned to sleep. In American usage, it refers to a specific personnel position, assignment, or duty station to which a soldier can be assigned. Historically, a billet was a private dwelling that was required to accept a soldier."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Vilhelm_Rosenstand_-_En_indkvarteringsscene_-_1898.png/330px-Vilhelm_Rosenstand_-_En_indkvarteringsscene_-_1898.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billet","wikidata":"Q1308509"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/The_Portuguese_Expeditionary_Corps_in_Britain%2C_1917-1918_Q30102.jpg/500px-The_Portuguese_Expeditionary_Corps_in_Britain%2C_1917-1918_Q30102.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/The_Portuguese_Expeditionary_Corps_in_Britain%2C_1917-1918_Q30102.jpg/1280px-The_Portuguese_Expeditionary_Corps_in_Britain%2C_1917-1918_Q30102.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/The_Portuguese_Expeditionary_Corps_in_Britain%2C_1917-1918_Q30102.jpg/500px-The_Portuguese_Expeditionary_Corps_in_Britain%2C_1917-1918_Q30102.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Troop